@@ -4016,6 +4016,25 @@ attribute:
     >>> Question.objects.prefetch_related(prefetch).get().choice_set.all()
     <QuerySet [<Choice: Not much>, <Choice: The sky>, <Choice: Just hacking again>]>
 
+The ``queryset`` can be :ref:`sliced <limiting-querysets>` to limit the number
+of related objects prefetched for each instance. For example, to prefetch the
+two most voted choices of each question:
+
+    >>> top_choices = Choice.objects.order_by('-votes')[:2]
+    >>> prefetch = Prefetch('choice_set', queryset=top_choices, to_attr='top_choices')
+    >>> Question.objects.prefetch_related(prefetch).get().top_choices
+    [<Choice: The sky>, <Choice: Not much>]
+
+The slice is applied to the related objects of each instance separately rather
+than to all prefetched objects as a whole. Prefetching from a sliced queryset
+is only supported for many-to-many, reverse many-to-one, and
+``GenericRelation`` relations on databases that support
+:ref:`window-functions`.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 4.2
+
+    Support for sliced querysets was added.
+
 .. note::
 
     When using ``to_attr`` the prefetched result is stored in a list. This can
